1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,815
Brain freeze has a real medical name: sphenopalatine ganglioneuralgia.

2
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:09,099
It starts when something very cold touches the roof of your mouth.

3
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:14,877
The cold makes blood vessels there narrow, then quickly widen again.

4
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:20,919
Nerves sense the sudden change and send a pain signal to the brain.

5
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:24,937
But your brain feels it in your forehead.

6
00:00:24,937 --> 00:00:26,483
This is called referred pain.

7
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:29,809
It fades in seconds.

8
00:00:29,809 --> 00:00:33,358
Press your tongue to the roof of your mouth, or sip lukewarm water.

9
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:38,910
Best prevention: enjoy cold treats slowly — small bites, small sips.
